From 9f937573df62e62f32a0e6345e33430e821d5f5a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: waydroid-nvidia-prolapse <build@local>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 00:57:16 +0300
Subject: [PATCH 06/29] hwcomposer: a lost Wayland connection ends the composer
 with a named cause
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=utf-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

What: when wl_display_dispatch() fails for good, hwc_wayland_thread() logs
the cause (protocol error interface/id/code, or the errno of the
disconnect), stores it in the property waydroid.hwc.wayland_lost and exits
the process with status 75 (HWC_EXIT_WAYLAND_LOST) via _exit(), instead of
abort().

Why: after the compositor connection is gone nothing the HAL draws can reach
the screen. The source (quinovax ad04e0a) removed this abort() by flagging
the display dead and returning, which leaves a composer that keeps answering
SurfaceFlinger while nothing is shown: a silent hang (principle 5). Here the
end is deliberate and observable: an error line with the cause, the
property, and init's restart of vendor.hwcomposer-2-1, after which every
start attempt that cannot reach the compositor logs "Couldn't open Wayland
display" / "failed to open hwcomposer device: No such device" every 5 s.
abort() ended the process the same way but as a crash (tombstone), with the
cause only in logcat. _exit() runs no user-space code (no destructors, no
atexit handlers).

Measured 2026-10-12 (nested cage compositor, stopped under the running
guest): "Wayland connection lost (disconnected: Broken pipe); hwcomposer
exits with status 75", waydroid.hwc.wayland_lost = "disconnected: Broken
pipe", no tombstone, init restarting the composer every 5 s.
Limits measured in the same run, independent of this patch:
- The session bind-mounts the compositor's socket file
  (config_session: /run/user/1000/wayland-N -> run/xdg/wayland-0), so a
  compositor that recreates its socket (new inode) cannot be reached again;
  a compositor that keeps serving the same socket (KWin's wrapper across
  KWin restarts) should be, not tested.
- init's onrestart of surfaceflinger does not take effect in the Waydroid
  container: "Sending signal 9 to service 'surfaceflinger' process group ...
  Successfully killed", yet the process stays alive and init.svc.surfaceflinger
  stays "stopping". So recovery needs a session restart; the host session
  could watch waydroid.hwc.wayland_lost to do it (not implemented).

Source: ours (principle 5), replacing the frozen-HAL hunk of QuinOvaX
  quinovax/waydroid-nvidia dev ad04e0a (hwc_wayland_thread / wayland_dead).
Licence: Apache-2.0 (android_hardware_waydroid).

保留 ATV 已实现的 ctl 重连和 task 连接独立回收，不使用退出 75 重启整个 HAL；移植命名错误原因、协议对象诊断与 waydroid.hwc.wayland_lost 属性，避免一个任务连接掉线终止所有任务。

(cherry picked from commit 62ffee8c086c200d0ce75ad1857d353defdadec3)
---
 hwcomposer/wayland-hwc.cpp | 16 ++++++++++++++++
 hwcomposer/wayland-hwc.h   |  1 +
 2 files changed, 17 insertions(+)

diff --git a/hwcomposer/wayland-hwc.cpp b/hwcomposer/wayland-hwc.cpp
index 0b3a3b9..e1298e8 100644
--- a/hwcomposer/wayland-hwc.cpp
+++ b/hwcomposer/wayland-hwc.cpp
@@ -3824,6 +3824,22 @@ static void* wl_conn_thread(void* data) {
             continue;
 
         conn->wl_alive = false;
+        if (!conn->stopping) {
+            char cause[PROPERTY_VALUE_MAX];
+            int err = wl_display_get_error(conn->display);
+            if (err == EPROTO) {
+                const struct wl_interface *iface = nullptr;
+                uint32_t id = 0;
+                uint32_t code = wl_display_get_protocol_error(conn->display, &iface, &id);
+                snprintf(cause, sizeof(cause), "protocol error: interface %s id %u code %u",
+                         iface ? iface->name : "?", id, code);
+            } else {
+                snprintf(cause, sizeof(cause), "disconnected: %s", strerror(err));
+            }
+            ALOGE("Wayland connection lost (ctl=%d task=%u): %s",
+                  conn->is_ctl, conn->task_id, cause);
+            property_set("waydroid.hwc.wayland_lost", cause);
+        }
 
         /* Torn down on purpose, or a task connection whose session is simply
          * gone: exit and let the joiner clean up. Only ctl is reconnected. */
diff --git a/hwcomposer/wayland-hwc.h b/hwcomposer/wayland-hwc.h
index 9c97a4b..9160969 100644
--- a/hwcomposer/wayland-hwc.h
+++ b/hwcomposer/wayland-hwc.h
@@ -831,6 +831,7 @@ handle_relative_motion(void *data, struct zwp_relative_pointer_v1*,
 void
 snapshot_inactive_app_window(struct display *display, struct window *window);
 
+
 struct display *
 create_display(const char* gralloc);
 void
